      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's helpful, thanks. I see the logic there. To balance it out for my paper, can you expand on the liberal side? Specifically, how do they frame the concept of 'dignity' in a way that isn't just 'it's my body, my choice'? I'm looking for the more robust theological justifications they use to claim that MAiD can actually be a moral or even a spiritual act.",
